# EVERY fixture here must be ENUMERATED on the out-of-profile path, never
# silently dropped and never merely counted -- a dropped axiom is an incoherence
# the reasoner subsequently cannot see. Each yields non-empty coverage.omitted,
# so the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2), never coherent.
# #
# ObjectOneOf and ObjectHasValue -- nominals, deferred and answered NO
# for the first consumer. Equality is what the nominal-free encoding lacks.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix swrl: <http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual . :b a owl:NamedIndividual .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Class ; owl:oneOf ( :a :b ) ] .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:hasValue :a ] .
